      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "•\tRedo Iterable<> ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "•\t                nonvirtual  void    Apply (void (*doToElement) (const T& item)) const;",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tUsuing std::function (template)? Maybe not needed? Test if Apply() works with lambdas? If not – consider using std::function  - but test if any size/performance penalty…",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tBut the SAME answer should apply to SimpleRunner – so test – can you do bind() and hten have THAT map to a C++ function – I think no. So you need to use std::function as the arg!!!",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
